e higher rates compared to budget apartments in less affluent areas.<\/li>\r\n<li><b style=\"font-size: 0.8125rem;\">Amenities<\/b>: The availability of amenities within a property complex or neighbourhood can significantly impact its value. Amenities like swimming pools, gyms, parks, security systems, and parking facilities can attract higher-paying tenants or buyers, thereby increasing property rates.<\/li>\r\n<li><b style=\"font-size: 0.8125rem;\">Demand and supply<\/b>: The basic economic principle of supply and demand heavily influences property rates. Areas experiencing high demand and limited supply are likely to have higher property rates, while those with oversupply and low demand may see stagnation or even decreases in rates.<\/li>\r\n<li><b style=\"font-size: 0.8125rem;\">Infrastructure development<\/b>: Infrastructure development projects such as new roads, highways, public transportation systems, airports, and commercial developments can boost property rates in nearby areas. Improved infrastructure enhances connectivity, accessibility, and overall livability, making properties in these areas more desirable and valuable.<\/li>\r\n<\/ol>\r\n",
